    "stem": "House $H$ and shop $S$ lie on the same side of straight path $L$. Ananya must walk from $H$ to a point $P$ on $L$, then to $S$, and wants the shortest broken path $H$-$P$-$S$. Point $S'$ is the reflection of $S$ across $L$.\n\nWhich claim correctly chooses $P$?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Take $P$ as the foot of the perpendicular from $H$ to $L$ alone, and ignore $S$ and $S'$.",
      "B": "Call the answer line only, with no choice of $P$ on $L$.",
      "C": "Join $H$ to $S'$ by a straight segment; let $P$ be where that segment meets $L$.",
      "D": "Reflection still chooses $P$ even when $S'$ is not the same distance from $L$ as $S$ is."
    },
